        <!-- Upgrading -->
        <section id="upgrading" class="mb-12 scroll-mt-24">
          <h2
            class="text-foreground mb-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] sm:text-[1.75rem]"
          >
            Upgrading from Type 1 to Type 2: What to Expect
          </h2>
          <div class="text-muted-foreground space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              If you've completed Type 1 and are ready to pursue Type 2, the
              process is more streamlined than starting fresh—but there are
              important timing and cost considerations.
            </p>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-foreground mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">
                Timing Your Type 2 Audit After Type 1
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-3">
                The ideal approach is to begin your Type 2 observation period
                immediately after your Type 1 audit closes. This means:
              </p>
              <ul class="ml-0 list-none space-y-2">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-muted-foreground">•</span>
                  <span>
                    Your Type 1 audit date becomes the start of your Type 2
                    observation period</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-muted-foreground">•</span>
                  <span>
                    You can have a Type 2 report ready 6-9 months after your
                    Type 1 report</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-muted-foreground">•</span>
                  <span>
                    Many auditors offer discounts when you use them for both
                    Type 1 and Type 2</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-muted-foreground">•</span>
                  <span>
                    The system description from your Type 1 report becomes the
                    baseline for Type 2</span
                  >
                </li>
              </ul>
              <p class="mt-3">
                Don't wait months after your Type 1 closes to start accumulating
                evidence—every delay extends your overall timeline to Type 2.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-foreground mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">
                Additional Evidence and Controls Needed
              </h3>
              <p class="mb-3">
                Moving from Type 1 to Type 2 primarily adds operational
                requirements, not new controls:
              </p>
              <ul class="ml-0 list-none space-y-2">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-muted-foreground">•</span>
                  <span
                    ><strong class="text-foreground"
                      >Evidence management system:</strong
                    >
                    You need systematic processes to capture and organize evidence
                    throughout the observation period</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-muted-foreground">•</span>
                  <span
                    ><strong class="text-foreground"
                      >Control operation consistency:</strong
                    >
                    Controls that existed on paper for Type 1 must now be demonstrably
                    executed on schedule</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <span class="text-muted-foreground">•</span>
                  <span
                    ><strong class="text-foreground">Historical records:</strong
                    >
                    Access reviews, change tickets, training logs—all must be captured
                    and retained throughout the observation period</span
                  >
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-foreground mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">
                Cost of Upgrade vs. Starting with Type 2
              </h3>
              <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
                  <thead>
                    <tr class="border-border-low border-b">
                      <th
                        class="text-foreground py-3 pr-4 text-left font-semibold"
                        >Path</th
                      >
                      <th
                        class="text-foreground py-3 pr-4 text-left font-semibold"
                        >Total Audit Cost</th
                      >
                      <th class="text-foreground py-3 text-left font-semibold"
                        >Time to Type 2 Report</th
                      >
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
